Fix DPD sweep's mandatory-town rejection, add Ireland, probe Friday (v0.139)

Dan's feedback on v0.138's new "Refresh from live lookup" sweep: it failed
outright on every single postcode, he wanted the Republic of Ireland added,
and he wanted the sweep to probe a Friday so Saturday/Sunday services show
up - plus he found 3 of the original sweep postcodes don't actually
validate against DPD.

Root cause of the total failure (DpdShippingService):
- refreshAllKnownServices() was calling fetchAvailableServicesRaw() with an
  empty string for every probe's delivery town. DPD's outboundservices
  endpoint enforces that field in practice ("Delivery city is mandatory
  (Delivery city)") even though its documented schema carries no mandatory
  asterisk on it - confirmed by browsing DPD's own live API docs
  (validate-outbound-services-for-address). SERVICE_SWEEP_POSTCODES is now
  {label, postcode, town, countryCode} instead of {label, postcode}, with a
  real town per entry, and refreshAllKnownServices() passes it through.

Postcode corrections, confirmed via doogal.co.uk (Royal Mail PAF lookup):
- Isle of Wight and Isles of Scilly's previous sweep postcodes were
  invented, not real addresses - replaced with PO30 1XY and TR21 0NS,
  both confirmed current and in PAF.
- Isle of Man's postcode is swapped to IM1 2LE, but Isle of Man doesn't
  appear to be in current Royal Mail PAF data at all (doogal has no
  individual postcode records for it) - likely why DPD may keep rejecting
  this one specific entry regardless of which postcode is tried. Flagged
  to Dan as a probable structural limitation, not promised as fixed.

Republic of Ireland (both couriers' sweeps):
- New entry using Dublin's GPO Eircode (D01 F5P2), town "Dublin", country
  code IE.

Collection date / Saturday-Sunday visibility:
- APC's ServiceAvailability.json does accept CollectionDate, so
  ApcShippingService's sweep now probes on the next available Friday
  (today if today is already a Friday - see the new nextFriday() helper)
  instead of always "today", giving Saturday/Sunday services a chance to
  actually appear. buildServiceAvailabilityBodyRaw() gained a
  collectionDate parameter for this.
- DPD's outboundservices endpoint has no date field anywhere in its schema
  at all (confirmed against the same live API docs) - there's nothing to
  change on the DPD side for this part of the request, so DPD's sweep is
  unaffected.

